{
  "id": "COMPOUND:31899 - PROTEIN:5805",
  "verbalization": "Nortoxiferine, dihydro- is implicated in the pathogenesis of SCCH-26 through a series of mechanistic links, primarily targeting the 26S proteasome non-ATPase regulatory subunit 14. This subunit is a known target of multiple compounds, including Nortoxiferine, which is also a target of WS-5995 B and 5alpha,6alpha-Epoxy(22e,24r)-ergosta-8(14),22-dien-3beta,7alpha-diol. These compounds are all linked to SCCH-26, suggesting a shared mechanism of action involving the proteasome pathway. The evidence supports a potential role for Nortoxiferine in modulating proteasome activity, which could influence cellular processes in SCCH-26 cells. The integration of these targets and their downstream effects implies that Nortoxiferine may exert its effects through a proteasome-dependent mechanism, potentially affecting cell survival or proliferation in SCCH-26. The observed scores suggest a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, but further validation through experimental studies would be necessary to confirm the precise mechanism and therapeutic relevance.",
